                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "overall in favor of this patch, since Tyan Header is already supported."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device/fru_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 755,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "We are duplicating the code here, but the only difference is the data in the header.\n\nWhat about making an `std::map<std::vector<uint8_t>, size_t>` which maps the header to the fru offset.\n\nThen just iterate over those keys and check if that header is present."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device/fru_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 755,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "making a std::map<std::vector> would allocate several extra times before doing the lookup.\n\nThis also technically allocates, ideally these would both be constexpr arrays, but I'll follow up with that in another patch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device/fru_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 755,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Alexander, that work for you?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device/fru_utils.cpp",
                    "line": 755,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes \ud83d\udc4d\n\nWe can duplicate here, then de-duplicate in a follow-up patch.\n\nIMO sometimes that's more readable than doing both at once."
                }
            ],
